 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b524258f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SSingle-band gap filling with a Neural Stochastic Flow\n",
    "\n",
    "Runs in the **jax** environment. Reads the `.npz` and never imports eztao to avoid dependency issues.\n",
    "\n",
    "Validate the learned transition against the analytic DRW -> gap-fill -> compare to the Bayes-optimal DRW-GP"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "38ed5650",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%load_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "import numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from jax import random\n",
    "\n",
    "from Style     import useAA          
    "from Tensorize import loadDataset\n",
    "from NSF       import makeModels, train, checkTransition\n",
    "from GapFill   import fillGaps, drwGPBaseline, gapWidths, coverage, plotGapFill\n",
    "\n",
    "useAA()\n",
    "DATA = \"/Users/anacecilialr/GitHub/MASS/MASS-Thesis/data\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load\n",
    "\n",
    "`loadDataset` normalises: $t \\to t/t_{max}$, $y \\to y/\\sigma$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note the validation set is loaded with the **training** scales. Letting it compute its own would leak validation statistics into the model's input distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "train (4000, 108)   val (1000, 102)\n",
      "tau_n = 0.0913  (= tau / t_max = 100 / 1095)\n",
      "sigma_n = 1.00,  max|y| = 5.42,  max t = 1.00\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "D = loadDataset(f\"{DATA}/train.npz\")\n",
    "V = loadDataset(f\"{DATA}/val.npz\", t_scale=D[\"t_scale\"], y_scale=D[\"y_scale\"])   # SAME scales\n",
    "\n",
    "tau_n, sig_n = float(D[\"tau\"][0]), float(D[\"sigma\"][0])\n",
    "print(f\"train {D['t'].shape}   val {V['t'].shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"tau_n = {tau_n:.4f}  (= tau / t_max = 100 / 1095)\")\n",
    "print(f\"sigma_n = {sig_n:.2f},  max|y| = {float(abs(D['y'][D['mask']]).max()):.2f},  max t = {float(D['t'].max()):.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Train\n",
    "\n",
    "Total loss (Kiyohara Eq. 11):\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L}(\\theta,\\xi) = \\underbrace{-\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathcal{D}}\\left[\\log p_\\theta(x_{t_j}\\mid x_{t_i})\\right]}_{\\mathcal{L}_{\\rm NLL}} + \\lambda\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\rm flow}(\\theta,\\xi)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Without **$\\mathcal{L}_{\\rm NLL}$** the model is trained only to be *self-consistent*, a property infinitely many wrong dynamics satisfy, and it never learns the DRW at all. Gap filling would still look plausible, because the bridge is conditioned on real endpoints at inference\n",
    "\n",
    "`lam = 0.1`: Kiyohara use 0.4 (Lorenz), find ~0.03 best (mocap), and report that\n",
    "sub-order-of-magnitude values suffice."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  step   100 | loss   1.9619\n",
      "  step   200 | loss   1.2135\n",
      "  step   300 | loss   1.1899\n",
      "  step   400 | loss   1.1764\n",
      "  step   500 | loss   1.1789\n",
      "  step   600 | loss   1.1769\n",
      "\n",
      "final loss 1.178   <- ~1-2 is healthy; ~50 means unnormalised data\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 650x286 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "flow, bridge = makeModels(random.PRNGKey(0))\n",
    "(flow, bridge), hist = train(flow, bridge, D, random.PRNGKey(1),\n",
    "                             steps=600, batch=16, lr=2e-3, lam=0.1, n_trip=32)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nfinal loss {np.mean(hist[-50:]):.3f}   <- ~1-2 is healthy; ~50 means unnormalised data\")\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(5, 2.2)); plt.plot(hist, lw=.5, color=\"tab:blue\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"step\"); plt.ylabel(\"loss\"); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "The true transition in closed form:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$X_t \\mid X_s \\;\\sim\\; \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(e^{-\\Delta t/\\tau}X_s,\\;\\; \\sigma^2\\left(1-e^{-2\\Delta t/\\tau}\\right)\\right)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "so the learned $p_\\theta(x_t\\mid x_s,\\Delta t)$ can be checked against it **directly**. Kiyohara could\n",
    "not do this on Lorenz or mocap. Important plot to add\n",
    "\n",
    "Run it before. **Mean must decay to 0; sd must saturate at $\\sigma$.**\n",
    "If either grows without bound, stop, the usual cause is unnormalized data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1040x377 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  mean @ 9 tau : -0.36  (analytic +0.00)   -> must decay to 0\n",
      "  sd   @ 9 tau : 1.07  (analytic 1.00)   -> must saturate at 1\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dts = np.logspace(np.log10(0.2*tau_n), np.log10(9*tau_n), 12)\n",
    "lm, lv, tm, tv = checkTransition(flow, tau_n, sig_n, 1.0, dts, random.PRNGKey(2), n=4000)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(8, 2.9))\n",
    "ax[0].axhline(0, color=\"0.85\", lw=.6)\n",
    "ax[0].plot(dts/tau_n, tm, \"k--\", label=r\"analytic  $e^{-\\Delta t/\\tau}x_s$\")\n",
    "ax[0].plot(dts/tau_n, lm, \"o-\", ms=3, color=\"tab:red\", label=\"learned NSF\")\n",
    "ax[0].set_ylabel(\"transition mean\")\n",
    "ax[1].axhline(sig_n, color=\"0.85\", lw=.6)\n",
    "ax[1].plot(dts/tau_n, np.sqrt(tv), \"k--\", label=r\"analytic  $\\sigma\\sqrt{1-e^{-2\\Delta t/\\tau}}$\")\n",
    "ax[1].plot(dts/tau_n, np.sqrt(lv), \"o-\", ms=3, color=\"tab:red\", label=\"learned NSF\")\n",
    "ax[1].set_ylabel(\"transition sd\")\n",
    "for a in ax: a.set_xscale(\"log\"); a.set_xlabel(r\"$\\Delta t/\\tau$\"); a.legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"  mean @ 9 tau : {lm[-1]:+.2f}  (analytic {tm[-1]:+.2f})   -> must decay to 0\")\n",
    "print(f\"  sd   @ 9 tau : {np.sqrt(lv[-1]):.2f}  (analytic {np.sqrt(tv[-1]):.2f})   -> must saturate at 1\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Gap filling, against the Bayes-optimal baseline\n",
    "\n",
    "The DRW-GP is handed the **true** $\\tau$ and $\\sigma$, and the data were generated from exactly that\n",
    "process, making it the optimal filler by construction. \n",
    "\n",
    "Filling a gap means conditioning on **both** endpoints, that is what a bridge is. The transition\n",
    "alone conditions on the left endpoint only, which is forecasting: it drifts and its band widens\n",
    "monotonically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "reconstructed on 1132 points from 88 observations\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "i = 0                                     # a curve the model has never seen\n",
    "m = np.asarray(V[\"mask\"][i])\n",
    "t_o, y_o, e_o = np.asarray(V[\"t\"][i])[m], np.asarray(V[\"y\"][i])[m], np.asarray(V[\"yerr\"][i])[m]\n",
    "t_tr, y_tr = np.asarray(V[\"t_true\"]), np.asarray(V[\"y_true\"][i])\n",
    "\n",
    "t_rec, s_rec = fillGaps(bridge, t_o, y_o, n_samples=200, grid_per_gap=12, seed=0)\n",
    "mu, sd = drwGPBaseline(t_o, y_o, e_o, t_rec, tau_n, sig_n)\n",
    "print(f\"reconstructed on {t_rec.size} points from {t_o.size} observations\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1170x806 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(9, 6.2), sharex=True)\n",
    "plotGapFill(t_tr, y_tr, t_o, y_o, e_o, t_rec, s_rec, ax=axes[0], label=\"NSF bridge\")\n",
    "plotGapFill(t_tr, y_tr, t_o, y_o, e_o, t_rec, (mu, mu-sd, mu+sd), ax=axes[1],\n",
    "            label=r\"DRW GP (oracle $\\tau,\\sigma$)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "                 coverage@68%      RMSE\n",
      "NSF bridge               0.65     0.199\n",
      "DRW-GP oracle            0.74     0.197\n",
      "\n",
      "(nominal coverage is 0.68; below it means the bands are too narrow)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "y_ref = np.interp(t_rec, t_tr, y_tr)                 # truth on the reconstruction grid\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n",
    "gp_s = mu[None, :] + sd[None, :] * rng.normal(size=(200, mu.size))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'':15s}{'coverage@68%':>14s}{'RMSE':>10s}\")\n",
    "for lab, s, med in [(\"NSF bridge\", s_rec, np.median(s_rec, 0)),\n",
    "                    (\"DRW-GP oracle\", gp_s, mu)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{lab:15s}{coverage(y_ref, s):>14.2f}{np.sqrt(np.mean((med-y_ref)**2)):>10.3f}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n(nominal coverage is 0.68; below it means the bands are too narrow)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Error vs gap size\n",
    "\n",
    "Bin by **gap width in units of $\\tau$**. Three 0.1 $\\tau$ gaps are not harder than one, they are three independent problems. The DRW forgets as $e^{-\\Delta t/\\tau}$, so $\\Delta t/\\tau$ is the only variable controlling how much information the endpoints carry, and it is what makes the axis comparable across curves once $\\tau$ varies.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1 of 1132 points lie outside the observed span (dropped: extrapolation)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 650x390 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "w = gapWidths(t_o, t_rec) / tau_n\n",
    "ok = np.isfinite(w)\n",
    "print(f\"{(~ok).sum()} of {ok.size} points lie outside the observed span (dropped: extrapolation)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "bins = np.logspace(-2, 0.7, 9); cen = np.sqrt(bins[:-1]*bins[1:])\n",
    "idx = np.digitize(w[ok], bins) - 1\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(5, 3))\n",
    "for lab, e, col in [(\"NSF bridge\", np.abs(np.median(s_rec, 0)-y_ref)[ok], \"tab:red\"),\n",
    "                    (\"DRW GP (oracle)\", np.abs(mu-y_ref)[ok], \"k\")]:\n",
    "    med = [np.median(e[idx == b]) if (idx == b).sum() > 3 else np.nan for b in range(len(cen))]\n",
    "    plt.plot(cen, med, \"o-\", ms=3, color=col, label=lab)\n",
    "plt.xscale(\"log\"); plt.yscale(\"log\"); plt.axvline(1.0, color=\"0.85\", lw=.6)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(r\"gap width / $\\tau$\"); plt.ylabel(r\"median $|$error$|$ / $\\sigma$\")\n",
    "plt.legend(fontsize=7); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next\n",
    "\n",
    "1. More steps?\n",
    "2. Coverage ~0.6 vs nominal 0.68 → bands too narrow. Sweep `lam`; Kiyohara report low\n",
    "   sensitivity around the right order of magnitude.\n",
    "3. Loop sections 4–5 over all 100 validation curves and report\n",
    "   distributions. One curve is an illustration, not a result.\n",
    "4. **Stage 2 with latent NSF.** Encoder + emission $p_\\psi(o\\mid x,\\mathrm{yerr})$ + $\\beta$-NELBO +\n",
    "   the skip-ahead KL (Eq. 17), Kiyohara's direct answer to long-gap degradation. Then multiband:\n",
    "   the transition kernel never changes, bands touch only the encoder and the emission."
   ]
  },
